{"id": "EUVD-2026-97496", "enisaUuid": "644decc6-5d05-3763-a43d-10aafc2a8745", "description": "SWUpdate through 2026.05.1 contains an improper certificate validation vulnerability in crypto/swupdate_cms_verify_openssl.c that trusts untrusted X.509 certificates embedded in CMS SignedData for chain building. Attackers holding a signing key from a sibling intermediate under the same root can embed that intermediate in the signature to install malicious updates.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T15:16:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:15", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://groups.google.com/g/swupdate/c/dsoMcGFnEns", "https://github.com/sbabic/swupdate/commit/e66c5640664a31668926a24c0c84b6b6570dc0d9", "https://github.com/sbabic/swupdate/blob/2026.05.1/crypto/swupdate_cms_verify_openssl.c", "https://github.com/sbabic/swupdate", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/swupdate-through-2026.05.1-cms-signature-verification-bypass-via-embedded-intermediates"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109399", "GHSA-xf8v-f779-856c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5f05433e-f56c-3ce0-b014-fb6e22503d1f", "product": {"name": "swupdate", "vendor": {"name": "sbabic"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642026.05.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d5ed4580-c825-3d51-96ae-0a8cd46bb336", "vendor": {"name": "sbabic"}}], "isExploited": false}